.\" Manual page for the DistroForge Qt desktop application.
.\" The surface list, the keyboard shortcut and the exit statuses documented
.\" here are derived from distroforge/ui/app.py, distroforge/ui/main_window.py
.\" and distroforge/ui/qt.py, not written from memory.
.TH distroforge\-gui 1 2026-07-26 "DistroForge 0.3.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
distroforge-gui \- launch the Qt desktop interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B distroforge\-gui
.RI [ QT\-OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B distroforge gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B distroforge\-gui
launches the DistroForge desktop application: the graphical counterpart of
.BR distroforge (1),
built on the same services and enforcing the same safety model. Builds stay
dry\-runs until execution is requested explicitly, privileged writes go through
the configured privilege helper, and no window action bypasses a check the CLI
performs.
.PP
The application takes no options of its own; it is a pure launcher. Anything on
the command line is handed to Qt, so the usual Qt platform arguments
.RB ( \-style ,
.BR \-platform ,
.BR \-stylesheet ,
.BR \-platformtheme )
are accepted. Project selection, options and actions all happen inside the
window.
.B distroforge gui
is the same launcher reached from the command\-line tool.
.PP
The window presents 15 surfaces, all reachable at any workflow level:
.BR Start ,
.BR Source ,
.BR Packages ,
.BR "Desktop & Identity" ,
.BR "Capture & Images" ,
.BR Presets ,
.BR "Quality Lab" ,
.BR "Virtualization Lab" ,
.BR Artifacts ,
.BR Maintainer ,
.BR "Command Center" ,
.BR Extensions ,
.BR "Advanced Modules" ,
.BR "Build & Release"
and
.BR Logs .
.PP
.B Start
is the guided journey spine: an ordered, level\-gated list of the build steps,
each routing to its focused panel with an
.B "Apply this step"
and
.B Check
pair.
.B "Command Center"
is the auditor view: the
.B "What do you want to achieve?"
goal hub, the CLI/GUI parity map, the product capability map, the build phase
contracts and the CLI equivalent of the current settings, so the automation
surface can be learned from the desktop app.
.PP
Chosen workflow level
.RB ( beginner ,
.BR power\-user ,
.BR maintainer ,
.BR developer )
gates only how much of the guided spine is unlocked. Navigation is never gated:
the header
.B "Open tool\(rq"
palette is a type\-to\-filter action index over every surface and every journey
step, focused with
.BR Ctrl+K ,
and a
.B Start
button at the leading edge of the header bar returns home from any surface.
.PP
Long work never blocks the interface: builds, dry\-runs, doctor runs, audits and
snapshots are dispatched onto a worker thread that reports weighted progress and
supports cancellation through the toolbar job controls.
.SH OPTIONS
.B distroforge\-gui
defines no options of its own. The following are the Qt arguments most often
useful here; the Qt documentation lists the full set.
.TP
.BI \-style " STYLE"
Select the Qt widget style.
.TP
.BI \-platform " PLATFORM"
Select the window\-system plugin, for example
.B wayland
or
.BR xcb .
Setting it to
.B offscreen
runs the shell headlessly, which is how the GUI smoke tests drive it.
.TP
.BI \-stylesheet " FILE"
Load an additional Qt stylesheet.
.PP
The application forces its own GNOME\-native presentation: Adwaita Sans
typography, the
.B Adwaita
icon theme, and light or dark surfaces following the host colour scheme. Those
choices come from the transcribed GNOME HIG palette rather than from the host
theme, so the look does not drift between desktop environments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window was opened and closed normally.
.TP
.B 2
No Qt Python bindings are installed. The launcher prints the packages to
install and exits without opening a window.
.PP
Any other status is the exit code Qt itself returned.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform plugin, honoured before
.BR \-platform .
.B offscreen
runs without a display.
.TP
.B DISTROFORGE_PRIVILEGE
Default privilege backend for the builds the window starts:
.BR sudo " (the default), "
.B pkexec
or
.BR none .
.TP
.B SUDO_ASKPASS
Graphical askpass helper. A build started from the desktop has no terminal, so
the privilege helper uses
.B "sudo \-A"
with this program. When none is available, preflight stops before the first
privileged command with setup guidance rather than hanging on an invisible
password prompt.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base of the preferences file; defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base of the build\-memory corpus read by the advisory panels; defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/distroforge/
Application preferences: chosen workflow level, chroot backend and other
persisted choices. Written atomically through a
.I .part
file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/distroforge/build\-memory.jsonl
Host\-owned build\-memory corpus summarised by the
.B "Show build memory"
readout. Appended only when a build actually runs.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/distroforge.desktop
Desktop entry that launches this program.
.TP
.I /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/distroforge.svg
Application icon.
.TP
.I PROJECT/project.json
The project the window opens; the same file the command\-line tool reads.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/distroforge/
Installed documentation, including the CLI/GUI parity contract.
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch the desktop application:
.PP
.EX
distroforge\-gui
.EE
.PP
Launch it through the command\-line tool:
.PP
.EX
distroforge gui
.EE
.PP
Force the Wayland platform plugin:
.PP
.EX
distroforge\-gui \-platform wayland
.EE
.PP
Run the shell headlessly, as the offscreen smoke tests do:
.PP
.EX
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen distroforge\-gui
.EE
.PP
Install the optional Qt bindings when the launcher reports they are missing:
.PP
.EX
sudo apt install python3\-pyqt6
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR distroforge (1),
.BR distroforge\-typer (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
See
.I /usr/share/doc/distroforge/docs/gui\-parity.md
for the command\-to\-surface mapping,
.I docs/ux\-cognitive\-ergonomics.md
for the interface contract and
.I docs/velocity\-responsiveness.md
for the responsiveness contract.
.SH BUGS
DistroForge 0.3.5 is alpha software. Review the plan the window shows before
executing a build, and prefer a dedicated build host or virtual machine.
.PP
DistroForge is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
Canonical. Ubuntu is mentioned solely as a compatible target distribution.
